[1.5999999999999996,"o","\r\n=== FINAL (4 iterations, 4 tool calls, answer) ===\r\nI found several reports related to security and observability in the internal database. Here are the titles and authors:\r\n\r\n1. **MCP Adoption in Enterprise Tooling** - K. Anderson\r\n2. **Guardrails for Indirect Prompt Injection** - K. Anderson\r\n3. **Read-Only SQL Interfaces for Agents** - J. Marlowe\r\n4. **Filesystem Sandboxing for Coding Agents** - L. Okafor\r\n5. **Rate Limiting AI Tool Surfaces** - J. Marlowe\r\n6. **Structured Logging for Agent Tool Calls** - L. Okafor\r\n7. **Vector Databases vs. Hybrid Retrieval** - K. Anderson\r\n8. **Streaming Tool Events to Operator Consoles** - J. Marlowe\r\n\r\nIn addition, I searched for MCP security best practices and summarized the findings in a document saved as `reports/demo-briefing.md`. The summary highlights several key resources and their contributions to MCP security:\r\n\r\n- Security guidelines and implementation strategies\r\n- Vulnerabilities and risk mitigation techniques\r\n- Focus on both traditional and AI-specific security concerns\r\n\r\nYou can refer to the saved document for the detailed summary.\r\n"]
